        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Chaining MTU warning ignores IPsec encryption overhead",
        "explanation": "The warning promises to cover 'encapsulation or encryption overhead', but it only checks WireGuard and tunnel MTU adaptation. IPsec also adds overhead to every packet, and NewConfiguration accounts for it via p.IPsec.Enabled(). So a CNI chaining setup with IPsec and no route MTU gets no warning, even though Pods there can hit the same fragmentation or black-hole problem.",
        "suggestion": "Add the IPsec case to the condition: `if p.WgConfig.Enabled() || p.IPsec.Enabled() || p.TunnelConfig.ShouldAdaptMTU() {`",
